  2 tools completed in 15.9s (2 ✓)

/config set temperature now accepts only 0.0–1.0, the range a run actually sends. Before, /config set temperature 1.5 was accepted and written to the config. After that, every run clamped it to 1.0 and printed a warning. Now the command refuses it with temperature 1.5 out of range (0.0–1.0): yoyo sends at most 1.0 and writes nothing. Build, all tests, clippy and fmt pass, and the change is committed as dedbd35.

• What changed (`src/config.rs`): the setter accepts a value only if the run's clamp (cli::clamped_temperature) leaves it unchanged. The 1.0 limit is still written in one place only, so the setter can't drift from what the run sends. NaN, inf and non-numbers are still refused. The help text for the setting now says (0.0–1.0).
• Test: temperature_set_range_is_the_range_the_run_sends accepts 0, 0.0, 0.7, 1 and 1.0, and checks the clamp leaves each one unchanged. It refuses 1.0001, 1.5 (the value from the issue), 2.0, -0.1, NaN, inf and abc, and checks the error message names the range. It failed before the fix and passes after it.
• Not tested on the built binary: yoyo config set refuses to run from the shell without a terminal, so the unit test is the only check for this path. The commit message says so.
• Docs: docs/src/configuration/models.md and installation.md already said 0.0–1.0. Nothing in src/, docs/src or README.md says 0.0–2.0 any more, so no doc edits were needed.
• File size: config.rs is now 4706 lines against its registered limit of 4696; that is within the size check's allowance and the check passes.
• Allowing values above 1.0 (not done here): I filed this as #1207 and the commit names it. It would mean a per-provider limit, since Anthropic only takes 0–1. The issue cites the OpenAI-compatible chat-completion spec on Hugging Face's docs ("between 0 and 2"), which I read in this session. I couldn't read OpenAI's own reference page.
